ect <MATH_0010> of <MATH_0011> over <MATH_0012>\nsuch that such that the composition <MATH_0013> is equal to <MATH_0014>.\nThis makes sense because objects of <MATH_0015> over <MATH_0016>\nare morphisms <MATH_0017>. By Groupoids in Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0003>\nwe may assume <MATH_0018> is given by a <MATH_0019>-descent datum <MATH_0020>\nrelative to an fppf covering <MATH_0021>.\nThe agreement of <MATH_0022> means that the diagrams\n<MATHSEG_0001>and<MATHSEG_0002>\nare commutative.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nOn the other hand, an object <MATH_0023> of <MATH_0024> over a scheme <MATH_0025> over <MATH_0026>\nby Groupoids in Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0004>\nis given by a <MATH_0027>-descent datum <MATH_0028>\nrelative to an fppf covering <MATH_0029>.\nSetting <MATH_0030> we see that\nthe diagrams\n<MATHSEG_0003>and<MATHSEG_0004>\nare commutative.\n\n<STRUCT_0005><STRUCT_0006>\nWith this notation in place, we define a functor\n<MATH_0031>\nby sending <MATH_0032> as above to the object\n<MATH_0033> where <MATH_0034>, where\n<MATH_0035> is the composition <MATH_0036>, and where\n<MATH_0037> is the composition <MATH_0038>.\nConversely, given an object <MATH_0039>\nof the right hand side we can send this to the object\n<MATH_0040> of the left hand side.\nWe omit the discussion of what to do with morphisms (works\nin exactly the same manner).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:19e43cae167283a1171d5495046c7f7f5ee3012fc8089f18848b733300c735fb", "unit_id": "tag:0DTG:proof"}
